1
00:00:00,032 --> 00:00:02,115
(shoes tapping)

2
00:00:03,199 --> 00:00:05,283
What are you waiting for?

3
00:00:05,367 --> 00:00:07,533
If you're gonna switch
then do it already.

4
00:00:12,367 --> 00:00:13,367
Something wrong, brat?

5
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:38,619
The Innate Domain's closed off.

6
00:00:38,702 --> 00:00:39,742
The special grade is dead.

7
00:00:40,202 --> 00:00:43,620
Now we just need
Itadori to return safely.

8
00:00:46,787 --> 00:00:50,620
Yeah, sorry but he isn't
going to be coming back.

9
00:00:52,703 --> 00:00:53,496
There's no reason to be scared.

10
00:00:53,579 --> 00:00:55,037
I'm in such a great
mood right now.

11
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:57,496
Let's just chat for a bit.

12
00:01:00,746 --> 00:01:01,996
The kid had it coming

13
00:01:02,079 --> 00:01:04,621
for just using me without
making any kind of a deal,

14
00:01:04,704 --> 00:01:05,830
and now it feels like,

15
00:01:05,914 --> 00:01:07,538
he's having some
trouble switching back

16
00:01:08,205 --> 00:01:10,956
but then no matter what he did,

17
00:01:11,038 --> 00:01:12,830
this would've ended up the same.

18
00:01:16,580 --> 00:01:19,665
So I've been thinking
about the different ways,

19
00:01:19,748 --> 00:01:20,748
I can do this.

20
00:01:25,957 --> 00:01:28,081
(laughs)

21
00:01:30,332 --> 00:01:31,374
What are you doing?

22
00:01:38,249 --> 00:01:40,540
I'm taking this brat a hostage.

23
00:01:40,624 --> 00:01:41,541
What do you mean?

24
00:01:41,625 --> 00:01:43,000
It's simple.

25
00:01:43,083 --> 00:01:45,000
See, I can live without this,

26
00:01:45,083 --> 00:01:46,683
but that ain't true
for your punk friend.

27
00:01:48,792 --> 00:01:51,333
Switching out with
me means he dies.

28
00:01:51,416 --> 00:01:55,251
Oh, and also for good measure.

29
00:02:00,084 --> 00:02:01,334
Sukuna's finger.

30
00:02:01,417 --> 00:02:02,334
That special grade
cursed spirit in there,

31
00:02:02,417 --> 00:02:04,376
must have swallowed it.

32
00:02:06,002 --> 00:02:09,543
And with that, I'm
now is free as a bird,

33
00:02:09,627 --> 00:02:10,770
and now you can be frightened

34
00:02:10,794 --> 00:02:14,335
because I'm about to kill
you just for the hell of it.

35
00:02:17,418 --> 00:02:20,628
And just like that, our
positions are now reversed.

36
00:02:25,836 --> 00:02:30,837
(Opening Theme Music)

37
00:03:58,219 --> 00:04:00,886
The only thing
granted equally to all,

38
00:04:00,970 --> 00:04:02,594
is an unfair reality.

39
00:04:15,012 --> 00:04:17,387
You don't get it, but I do.

40
00:04:17,470 --> 00:04:20,054
Itadori is coming back,

41
00:04:20,972 --> 00:04:22,554
even if that means he'll die,

42
00:04:23,429 --> 00:04:24,888
that's just who he is.

43
00:04:24,972 --> 00:04:26,513
You give him too much credit.

44
00:04:26,596 --> 00:04:29,096
He's just a little tougher
and a whole lot denser

45
00:04:29,179 --> 00:04:31,347
than other human beings are.

46
00:04:31,430 --> 00:04:32,573
You should've seen
him a minute ago.

47
00:04:32,597 --> 00:04:36,722
He was scared out of his
mind and about to lose it.

48
00:04:36,806 --> 00:04:40,889
Prattling on about his
regrets and all that nonsense.

49
00:04:40,973 --> 00:04:43,306
So it's obvious the guy
doesn't have the guts

50
00:04:43,390 --> 00:04:44,640
to kill himself.

51
00:04:46,056 --> 00:04:47,640
His left hand's been restored.

52
00:04:55,182 --> 00:04:56,391
Healing.

53
00:04:56,474 --> 00:04:58,557
He can use reverse
curse techniques

54
00:04:58,641 --> 00:05:00,307
and Sukuna's incarnated.

55
00:05:00,391 --> 00:05:02,557
So even though he
can live without a heart,

56
00:05:02,641 --> 00:05:05,307
it should still be
damaging to him.

57
00:05:06,558 --> 00:05:09,392
I'll make sure he heals that
heart before Itadori returns.

58
00:05:09,475 --> 00:05:11,934
I just have to convince
him he can't beat me

59
00:05:12,017 --> 00:05:13,350
without a heart in his body.

60
00:05:14,684 --> 00:05:16,225
But can I do that?

61
00:05:18,309 --> 00:05:20,142
I froze up when that
other special-grade

62
00:05:20,226 --> 00:05:21,226
was in front of me.

63
00:05:25,226 --> 00:05:28,393
It's not about
whether I can do it,

64
00:05:28,476 --> 00:05:29,893
I have to do it.

65
00:05:34,644 --> 00:05:36,411
Oh, it feels so good to
be back outside again.

66
00:05:36,435 --> 00:05:39,352
Let's use all this open space.

67
00:05:39,435 --> 00:05:41,477
(grunts)

68
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:47,770
How interesting.

69
00:05:47,853 --> 00:05:49,645
You can use your Shikigami,

70
00:05:49,728 --> 00:05:52,144
but you still come
at me yourself.

71
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:55,646
(grunts)

72
00:05:58,688 --> 00:06:00,521
Give me more.

73
00:06:02,104 --> 00:06:03,145
And more.

74
00:06:08,689 --> 00:06:11,272
Put more curse behind it,

75
00:06:12,605 --> 00:06:14,522
when you strike me.

76
00:06:14,605 --> 00:06:16,730
(laughs)

77
00:06:18,564 --> 00:06:23,564
Orochi.

78
00:06:24,564 --> 00:06:26,564
Gang up on him now.

79
00:06:38,649 --> 00:06:41,107
Now, what did I say?

80
00:06:42,107 --> 00:06:43,900
Let's use the open space.

81
00:07:08,443 --> 00:07:11,235
It's not even a
matter of jujutsu,

82
00:07:11,318 --> 00:07:13,694
his power and his agility
are on a different level.

83
00:07:13,777 --> 00:07:16,318
That's a nice technique there.

84
00:07:16,402 --> 00:07:17,568
(grunts)

85
00:07:27,778 --> 00:07:29,528
Now what?

86
00:07:30,821 --> 00:07:34,153
I used up one of my Shikigami
to escape that Innate Domain.

87
00:07:35,696 --> 00:07:39,112
Demon Dog White and
Orochi are both destroyed

88
00:07:39,195 --> 00:07:40,654
and Nue's at his limit.

89
00:07:42,404 --> 00:07:44,822
I should release him before
he gets destroyed too.

90
00:07:49,863 --> 00:07:51,280
I get it now.

91
00:07:51,363 --> 00:07:55,948
You use the shadows
to create your Shikigami.

92
00:07:56,031 --> 00:07:58,406
It makes no difference
if he knows that now.

93
00:07:59,197 --> 00:08:00,489
So what's it to you?

94
00:08:02,031 --> 00:08:04,614
It's not a generic
technique that uses charms,

95
00:08:04,698 --> 00:08:07,782
it's adaptable as well.

96
00:08:07,865 --> 00:08:10,740
There's just one
thing I don't get.

97
00:08:10,824 --> 00:08:13,490
Why did you run back then?

98
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:18,407
Kind of a waste of your talents.

99
00:08:18,825 --> 00:08:20,700
Whatever.

100
00:08:22,241 --> 00:08:25,241
Either way that certainly
won't be enough to fix this.

101
00:08:25,324 --> 00:08:27,157
So he's figured it out.

102
00:08:27,241 --> 00:08:28,717
Risking your life
for meaningless shit.

103
00:08:28,741 --> 00:08:32,492
This punk isn't even close
to being worth the effort.

104
00:08:34,867 --> 00:08:36,659
[Itadori] Why'd you
bother saving me then?

105
00:08:41,659 --> 00:08:44,201
[Megumi] The only thing
granted equally to all,

106
00:08:44,285 --> 00:08:45,910
is an unfair reality.

107
00:08:49,910 --> 00:08:51,994
If I have the time
to curse someone,

108
00:08:52,076 --> 00:08:54,618
I'd rather spend it
thinking about people I love.

109
00:08:55,703 --> 00:08:56,845
[Megumi] There was
never any doubt as to

110
00:08:56,869 --> 00:08:59,536
what a good person she was.

111
00:09:00,786 --> 00:09:02,786
She deserved happiness
more than anyone ever did,

112
00:09:04,744 --> 00:09:06,912
but Tsumiki was still cursed.

113
00:09:10,662 --> 00:09:12,829
While the father
who named Megumi,

114
00:09:12,912 --> 00:09:15,203
with no regard for my gender,

115
00:09:15,287 --> 00:09:17,704
is still off somewhere
living as he pleases.

116
00:09:22,746 --> 00:09:24,746
Karma isn't fully automatic.

117
00:09:27,746 --> 00:09:30,079
Evil people are only
judged under the law.

118
00:09:32,789 --> 00:09:35,747
Jujutsu sorcerers
are just another cog

119
00:09:35,831 --> 00:09:38,372
in that machine of retribution.

120
00:09:40,914 --> 00:09:43,748
I want good people
to enjoy fairness,

121
00:09:43,832 --> 00:09:46,206
even if only a few will.

122
00:09:51,164 --> 00:09:53,748
And so, I save people unequally.

123
00:10:01,874 --> 00:10:03,541
That's the way.

124
00:10:03,624 --> 00:10:05,833
So this is when you start
burning through your life.

125
00:10:06,791 --> 00:10:07,834
Now I see.

126
00:10:08,834 --> 00:10:11,750
Well, in that case,

127
00:10:13,125 --> 00:10:16,001
Megumi, show me what you got.

128
00:10:18,709 --> 00:10:22,459
Sacred treasure, swing and ring,

129
00:10:22,543 --> 00:10:23,584
ring Eight Grip.

130
00:10:30,002 --> 00:10:31,669
Oh and just so you know,

131
00:10:33,669 --> 00:10:36,585
I didn't have any logical
reason for saving you back then.

132
00:10:38,544 --> 00:10:39,704
Even though it was dangerous,

133
00:10:39,752 --> 00:10:42,585
I just couldn't bear to see
a good person like you die.

134
00:10:42,669 --> 00:10:44,253
Sure I had my reservations,

135
00:10:44,753 --> 00:10:48,586
but ultimately I did it for
selfish emotional reasons,

136
00:10:50,211 --> 00:10:52,253
but that's fine though.

137
00:10:54,211 --> 00:10:55,212
I'm a jujutsu sorcerer.

138
00:10:57,546 --> 00:10:58,587
I'm not a hero.

139
00:11:00,212 --> 00:11:01,254
In all this time,

140
00:11:02,379 --> 00:11:04,379
I've never once
regretted saving you.

141
00:11:11,088 --> 00:11:12,630
Right,

142
00:11:12,714 --> 00:11:14,964
you're really a pretty
smart guy Fushiguro.

143
00:11:15,047 --> 00:11:17,714
I know you've put a
lot of thought into this.

144
00:11:17,797 --> 00:11:19,756
I think your conviction
is a good one,

145
00:11:20,881 --> 00:11:23,089
but I don't think mine
is exactly wrong either.

146
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:29,965
Sorry, I guess I'm done for.

147
00:11:30,048 --> 00:11:32,966
At least I won't be here
worrying about you anymore,

148
00:11:33,049 --> 00:11:35,424
or Kugisaki or Gojou.

149
00:11:36,924 --> 00:11:40,008
I hope you live a long life.

150
00:11:41,632 --> 00:11:44,300
(dramatic music)

151
00:12:06,926 --> 00:12:10,343
(upbeat music)

152
00:12:28,511 --> 00:12:29,761
Well, you're gonna tell me,

153
00:12:29,845 --> 00:12:31,929
what possibly could
have been so important

154
00:12:32,013 --> 00:12:36,262
that you decided to use a
precious finger on Sukuna?

155
00:12:36,345 --> 00:12:38,721
Tried to see how strong he is?

156
00:12:38,804 --> 00:12:42,387
Well, the test was half
baked, I'll admit that,

157
00:12:43,555 --> 00:12:44,864
but we did still
learn a few things.

158
00:12:44,888 --> 00:12:48,388
I can only pray
that's not an excuse.

159
00:12:49,513 --> 00:12:51,596
(mumbles)

160
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:52,805
Stop talking already,

161
00:12:52,888 --> 00:12:57,264
no one can understand you.

162
00:12:57,347 --> 00:12:59,472
Yet the meaning flows
right into our minds.

163
00:12:59,556 --> 00:13:00,889
It creeps me out.

164
00:13:07,347 --> 00:13:09,432
Hello and welcome.

165
00:13:09,515 --> 00:13:11,473
Would you like a
table for one, sir?

166
00:13:13,557 --> 00:13:14,473
Yes, thank you.

167
00:13:14,557 --> 00:13:15,598
One for lunch.

168
00:13:26,058 --> 00:13:28,099
I told them that if
they encountered one,

169
00:13:28,182 --> 00:13:31,559
their choices were
either run or die.

170
00:13:31,642 --> 00:13:32,559
I specifically warned them

171
00:13:32,642 --> 00:13:35,642
that fighting was
absolutely not an option.

172
00:13:38,018 --> 00:13:39,892
It was intentional huh?

173
00:13:39,976 --> 00:13:41,559
What do you mean by that?

174
00:13:42,559 --> 00:13:44,000
The special grade
sending first years

175
00:13:44,060 --> 00:13:46,935
to rescue five people
who may already be dead,

176
00:13:47,019 --> 00:13:49,476
should have been
out of the question.

177
00:13:49,560 --> 00:13:50,310
Besides with Yuuji,

178
00:13:50,393 --> 00:13:52,768
I was the one who
forced the issue

179
00:13:52,852 --> 00:13:55,019
and got the kid's execution
sentence suspended.

180
00:13:55,101 --> 00:13:57,811
Some higher-ups
didn't like that,

181
00:13:57,894 --> 00:14:00,686
and so they took
advantage of my absence

182
00:14:00,769 --> 00:14:03,477
and used the special
grade to dispose of Yuuji.

183
00:14:04,394 --> 00:14:06,185
If the other two
had died as well,

184
00:14:06,269 --> 00:14:08,062
it'd mean more trouble for me,

185
00:14:08,145 --> 00:14:10,185
and they would have killed
two birds with one stone.

186
00:14:10,228 --> 00:14:14,812
Yeah, but wait, when the
initial dispatch went out,

187
00:14:14,895 --> 00:14:17,562
no one knew it would
become a special grade.

188
00:14:17,645 --> 00:14:19,896
Trying to pin the
blame is such a pain.

189
00:14:21,146 --> 00:14:23,396
Maybe I ought to
just cut to the chase

190
00:14:24,896 --> 00:14:27,604
and go kill off all
those higher-ups.

191
00:14:30,229 --> 00:14:33,522
You're not usually
this emotional.

192
00:14:33,605 --> 00:14:35,023
Good to see you, Miss Ieiri.

193
00:14:36,188 --> 00:14:38,230
Sounds to me,

194
00:14:38,314 --> 00:14:40,522
like you took quite
a liking to this one.

195
00:14:41,023 --> 00:14:42,856
I've always been the kind of guy

196
00:14:42,939 --> 00:14:44,189
who cares about his students.

197
00:14:44,273 --> 00:14:47,189
Regardless, you shouldn't
torment Ijichi too much.

198
00:14:47,273 --> 00:14:51,106
It's hard for him to be stuck
between us and the higher-ups.

199
00:14:51,189 --> 00:14:53,398
Yes, I don't care about
another man's hardships.

200
00:14:53,481 --> 00:14:54,565
Keep going, keep going.

201
00:14:54,648 --> 00:14:55,858
Is that so?

202
00:14:56,107 --> 00:15:01,524
So this here is
Sukuna's vessel huh?

203
00:15:04,316 --> 00:15:06,025
I can cut him up, yes?

204
00:15:06,107 --> 00:15:08,067
Just make good use of him.

205
00:15:08,150 --> 00:15:09,150
Oh I will.

206
00:15:10,233 --> 00:15:12,525
Who do you think I am?

207
00:15:17,984 --> 00:15:20,151
He said live a long life?

208
00:15:21,526 --> 00:15:23,776
Guess that doesn't mean
much when you die yourself.

209
00:15:24,192 --> 00:15:27,484
First time having a
partner of yours die on you?

210
00:15:28,234 --> 00:15:29,359
-One my age?
-Yeah.

211
00:15:32,360 --> 00:15:33,986
You're taking it well though.

212
00:15:34,694 --> 00:15:35,610
Yeah, you too.

213
00:15:35,694 --> 00:15:37,444
Well, of course.

214
00:15:37,527 --> 00:15:40,069
Two weeks ago, I
didn't even know him.

215
00:15:40,152 --> 00:15:43,610
I'm not the type to break
down and fall to pieces,

216
00:15:43,694 --> 00:15:45,361
when a guy I barely know dies.

217
00:15:47,153 --> 00:15:49,278
I mean, jeez.

218
00:16:00,779 --> 00:16:01,946
It's hot, huh?

219
00:16:04,571 --> 00:16:07,237
Yeah, wonder if it's time
for summer uniforms.

220
00:16:16,530 --> 00:16:17,613
So what's this?

221
00:16:19,530 --> 00:16:22,448
You're looking even more
bummed-out than usual, Megumi.

222
00:16:22,531 --> 00:16:23,531
Having a wake?

223
00:16:24,114 --> 00:16:26,656
What's up Zenin?

224
00:16:26,740 --> 00:16:28,489
Stop calling me by my last name.

225
00:16:28,573 --> 00:16:29,489
Maki, Maki.

226
00:16:29,573 --> 00:16:30,114
Hey I'm talking here, shut it.

227
00:16:30,197 --> 00:16:32,449
Are you serious right now?

228
00:16:32,532 --> 00:16:34,449
You don't know why
they're so down now?

229
00:16:34,532 --> 00:16:35,824
No, should I?

230
00:16:35,907 --> 00:16:38,324
Someone died yesterday, a boy.

231
00:16:38,407 --> 00:16:40,115
He was one of the first years.

232
00:16:40,198 --> 00:16:41,240
Bonito flakes.

233
00:16:41,324 --> 00:16:43,866
Well, why didn't you say so?

234
00:16:43,949 --> 00:16:45,783
Now I look like some
kind of heartless,

235
00:16:45,867 --> 00:16:47,158
cold-blooded ice-demon

236
00:16:47,241 --> 00:16:48,992
Yeah, that's how you came off.

237
00:16:49,075 --> 00:16:49,992
Tuna and mayo.

238
00:16:50,075 --> 00:16:51,592
-Don't say that.
-So who are these guys?

239
00:16:51,616 --> 00:16:53,700
You're supposed to try
to make me feel better.

240
00:16:53,783 --> 00:16:54,825
The second years.

241
00:16:55,950 --> 00:16:58,326
You have to try to be
kinder to your underclassmen.

242
00:16:58,409 --> 00:17:01,367
Hey, being soft on them
isn't gonna help them.

243
00:17:01,451 --> 00:17:03,534
[Megumi] Zenin is the
best of all the students

244
00:17:03,617 --> 00:17:05,534
at wielding curse tools.

245
00:17:05,617 --> 00:17:06,659
Salmon roe.

246
00:17:06,743 --> 00:17:08,135
[Megumi] And that's the
Cursed Speech user, Inumaki.

247
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:11,077
He can only speak in
ingredients of rice balls.

248
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:15,493
He is a little bit softer
whenever Yuuta's around though.

249
00:17:15,577 --> 00:17:16,327
And that's Panda.

250
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:18,702
There's one more.

251
00:17:18,785 --> 00:17:20,160
His name is Okkotsu,

252
00:17:20,244 --> 00:17:23,244
and he's actually the only
second year I genuinely respect.

253
00:17:24,995 --> 00:17:26,369
But he's overseas right now.

254
00:17:26,453 --> 00:17:27,578
Panda?

255
00:17:27,661 --> 00:17:29,328
That's all you're
giving me is Panda.

256
00:17:29,411 --> 00:17:32,787
Sorry to hit you up with this
now when you're in mourning.

257
00:17:32,871 --> 00:17:34,537
Bad timing.

258
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:36,038
Please forgive us for that.

259
00:17:37,495 --> 00:17:38,513
But see, we'd like you both

260
00:17:38,537 --> 00:17:41,662
to be in the Kyoto Sister
School Exchange Event.

261
00:17:42,871 --> 00:17:44,913
Kyoto Sister School
Exchange Event?

262
00:17:46,288 --> 00:17:47,913
What is that?

263
00:17:47,997 --> 00:17:50,663
It's a get-together with the
other Tech school in Kyoto,

264
00:17:51,496 --> 00:17:52,747
but isn't that event mainly

265
00:17:52,830 --> 00:17:54,621
for second and
third year students?

266
00:17:55,997 --> 00:17:58,539
Turns out the idiot third years
got themselves suspended,

267
00:17:58,622 --> 00:18:00,789
so you need to participate.

268
00:18:00,873 --> 00:18:02,432
So what exactly do
you do at this event?

269
00:18:02,456 --> 00:18:04,581
Smash bros?

270
00:18:04,664 --> 00:18:06,414
I rule at the Wii version.

271
00:18:06,497 --> 00:18:08,164
I'll Meteor Smash your butts.

272
00:18:09,082 --> 00:18:11,248
We'll make a three man team.

273
00:18:11,332 --> 00:18:12,349
The whole event
starts with the principals

274
00:18:12,373 --> 00:18:15,457
of the Tokyo and Kyoto schools.

275
00:18:15,540 --> 00:18:17,957
Each principal proposes
a form of competition

276
00:18:18,041 --> 00:18:19,832
that will be held
for an entire day,

277
00:18:19,915 --> 00:18:22,166
over the course of two days.

278
00:18:22,249 --> 00:18:24,333
At least that's how
it's supposed to go.

279
00:18:24,416 --> 00:18:26,042
It goes like this.

280
00:18:26,124 --> 00:18:28,416
Day one's team battles and
day two's individual battles.

281
00:18:28,499 --> 00:18:30,291
Salmon.

282
00:18:30,374 --> 00:18:33,250
Team battles and individual?

283
00:18:34,334 --> 00:18:36,417
You mean we fight
other jujutsu sorcerers.

284
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:39,250
Yeah, they're jujutsu battles

285
00:18:39,334 --> 00:18:41,542
where anything short
of killing is fair game.

286
00:18:42,500 --> 00:18:43,250
Don't worry, we'll train you up.

287
00:18:43,334 --> 00:18:45,918
So you probably
won't get killed.

288
00:18:48,543 --> 00:18:51,460
Do we have enough
jujutsu sorcerers?

289
00:18:51,543 --> 00:18:53,126
I thought we were really short.

290
00:18:53,209 --> 00:18:54,668
Do you have the time?

291
00:18:54,752 --> 00:18:56,002
Hey, good question.

292
00:18:56,961 --> 00:18:58,627
For now we're good.

293
00:18:58,711 --> 00:19:00,377
The dark emotions people harbor

294
00:19:00,461 --> 00:19:02,003
from late winter through spring,

295
00:19:02,086 --> 00:19:04,669
cause an outburst of
curses in early summer,

296
00:19:04,753 --> 00:19:06,836
so that's our busy season.

297
00:19:06,919 --> 00:19:08,294
Sometimes we're
busy all year long,

298
00:19:08,377 --> 00:19:11,128
but things should be settling
down here soon enough.

299
00:19:11,211 --> 00:19:12,670
Yeah?

300
00:19:12,754 --> 00:19:14,378
So are you in?

301
00:19:14,462 --> 00:19:16,503
I understand your
partner just died.

302
00:19:16,587 --> 00:19:18,004
-We're in.
-We're in.

303
00:19:18,087 --> 00:19:19,128
Cause I...

304
00:19:19,211 --> 00:19:20,211
Cause I...

305
00:19:21,379 --> 00:19:22,838
Have to get stronger

306
00:19:22,921 --> 00:19:25,838
and I'll do anything
to achieve that.

307
00:19:25,921 --> 00:19:28,880
But if I decide your training
exchange event is pointless,

308
00:19:28,963 --> 00:19:30,171
I'll quit instantly.

309
00:19:30,254 --> 00:19:31,254
Same here.

310
00:19:31,338 --> 00:19:33,547
Well, people this corky,

311
00:19:33,630 --> 00:19:35,380
are all the more
worthwhile to train.

312
00:19:35,464 --> 00:19:37,964
Bonito flakes.

313
00:19:39,422 --> 00:19:41,922
So you're saying that your boss,

314
00:19:42,006 --> 00:19:44,255
wants to reverse the
current relative positions

315
00:19:44,339 --> 00:19:46,340
of humans and curses.

316
00:19:46,423 --> 00:19:47,340
Is that right?

317
00:19:47,423 --> 00:19:50,715
Yeah, that's pretty close,

318
00:19:50,798 --> 00:19:51,918
but it's slightly different.

319
00:19:52,590 --> 00:19:55,923
Humans are
practically made of lies,

320
00:19:56,007 --> 00:19:58,883
for every positive action
and emotion they show,

321
00:19:58,966 --> 00:20:01,424
there's always a flip side,

322
00:20:01,507 --> 00:20:02,608
and yet negative emotions like

323
00:20:02,632 --> 00:20:05,466
hatred and hostility are
truths without falsehood.

324
00:20:08,215 --> 00:20:11,759
Since we curses are born
from those raw true emotions,

325
00:20:11,842 --> 00:20:15,092
that makes us true pure beings.

326
00:20:15,175 --> 00:20:17,967
Imitation should be eliminated.

327
00:20:18,051 --> 00:20:18,925
Yet at the moment,

328
00:20:19,009 --> 00:20:21,968
you're the ones who
are getting eliminated.

329
00:20:22,052 --> 00:20:23,485
And that's why we've
come here to ask you,

330
00:20:23,509 --> 00:20:27,760
what can we do to defeat
the jujutsu sorcerers?

331
00:20:27,843 --> 00:20:32,718
If you want to win, you'll
need to fulfill two conditions.

332
00:20:32,802 --> 00:20:34,886
Good, what are these conditions?

333
00:20:35,469 --> 00:20:39,469
The first thing, concerns
the strongest sorcerer.

334
00:20:39,552 --> 00:20:43,927
You must somehow render
Satoru Gojou incapable of fighting.

335
00:20:44,011 --> 00:20:46,595
The second, is to
get Ryoumen Sukuna

336
00:20:46,678 --> 00:20:48,470
and Yuuji Itadori on your side.

337
00:20:50,845 --> 00:20:53,803
But hold on a minute,
he died, didn't he?

338
00:20:53,887 --> 00:20:56,345
Wait, that Yuuji
Itadori, he's dead.

339
00:20:56,428 --> 00:20:58,763
Yeah?

340
00:20:58,846 --> 00:20:59,846
Did he die?

341
00:21:00,721 --> 00:21:02,262
I'm not so sure.

342
00:21:06,346 --> 00:21:07,763
Don't poke around inside me

343
00:21:07,846 --> 00:21:11,430
without my permission, punk-ass.

344
00:21:15,847 --> 00:21:20,847
(Closing Theme Music)

345
00:22:45,605 --> 00:22:47,064
[Both] Juju Stroll.

346
00:22:47,146 --> 00:22:48,188
[Toge] Salmon.

347
00:22:48,772 --> 00:22:49,897
[Maki] You stink.

348
00:22:49,980 --> 00:22:51,355
[Panda] I don't stink.

349
00:22:51,772 --> 00:22:53,897
[Maki] You stink.

350
00:22:53,980 --> 00:22:54,980
I do not stink.

351
00:22:55,563 --> 00:22:58,314
Why you be so mean?

352
00:22:58,397 --> 00:23:00,481
You're treating
you like an animal.

353
00:23:00,564 --> 00:23:01,647
Because you're a Panda.

354
00:23:01,731 --> 00:23:02,898
Mustard leaf.

355
00:23:02,981 --> 00:23:04,898
And you smell like an animal.

356
00:23:04,981 --> 00:23:06,790
I keep telling you to
take a bath, but you don't.

357
00:23:06,814 --> 00:23:10,107
I don't mind getting all wet.

358
00:23:10,190 --> 00:23:12,482
Unlike you humans all us
panda bears don't sweat,

359
00:23:12,565 --> 00:23:14,732
but I Febreze every day.

360
00:23:14,815 --> 00:23:17,815
So I know I don't stick.

361
00:23:23,733 --> 00:23:24,483
Here's your first task,

362
00:23:24,566 --> 00:23:26,566
step up and take a whiff.

363
00:23:26,649 --> 00:23:29,775
(sniffing)

364
00:23:36,817 --> 00:23:38,192
He doesn't really stink.

365
00:23:38,275 --> 00:23:40,525
Actually, Panda sort
of smells like the sun.

366
00:23:42,901 --> 00:23:44,984
-Sunshine.
-Sunshine.

367
00:23:45,068 --> 00:23:47,651
(upbeat music)

